#TODO: Update the unit test with new Scenario
Feature: Delete Policy

  Background:
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ",
         "name": "FAQ",
         "description": "FAQ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "tags": [
            "tags1",
            "tags2"
         ]
      }
      """
    And a Policy for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY_DEL",
         "description": "FAQ resource policy for Admin",
         "resourceType": "FAQ",
         "scope": "",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "roles": [
            "ADMIN-D1"
         ],
         "effect": "ALLOW"
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: delete Policy by Key
    When Resource Admin wants to delete the Policy with key 'FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY_DEL' and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    Then the Policy deleted successfully with response code 204

  Scenario: Positive: delete Policy with an existing/duplicate key but with different project
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57722' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ",
         "name": "FAQ",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 2",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "tags": ["tag1", "tag2"]
      }
      """
    And a Policy for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57722' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY",
         "description": "FAQ resource policy for Admin",
         "resourceType": "FAQ",
         "scope": "",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "roles": [
            "ADMIN-D1"
         ],
         "effect": "ALLOW"
      }
      """
    When Resource Admin wants to delete the Policy with key 'FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY' and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57722'
    Then the Policy deleted successfully with response code 204

  Scenario: Negative: delete Policy by a non-existent Key
    When Resource Admin wants to delete the Policy with key "FailKey" and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    Then the Policy deletion fails with response code 404
    And the response body includes status 404 and error message 'Not Found'
